  "description": "Available debugger operations.\n\nOperations:\n- list_checkpoints: List all active VICE checkpoints (breakpoints). Required inputs: none.\n- get_checkpoint: Fetch a single checkpoint by id. Required inputs: id.\n- create_checkpoint: Create a new checkpoint (breakpoint) in VICE. Required inputs: address. Optional inputs: endAddress, stopOnHit, enabled, temporary, label, operations, memspace.\n- delete_checkpoint: Remove a checkpoint by id. Required inputs: id.\n- toggle_checkpoint: Enable or disable a checkpoint by id. Required inputs: id, enabled.\n- set_condition: Attach a conditional expression to a checkpoint. Required inputs: id, expression.\n- list_registers: List available registers (metadata). Required inputs: none. Optional inputs: memspace.\n- get_registers: Read register values, optionally filtered by name or id. Required inputs: none. Optional inputs: memspace, registers.\n- set_registers: Write register values. Required inputs: writes. Optional inputs: memspace.\n- step: Single-step CPU execution. Required inputs: none. Optional inputs: count, mode.\n- step_return: Continue execution until the current routine returns. Required inputs: none.\n- get_monitor_state: Read CPU registers and return the current monitor state. Required inputs: none. Optional inputs: memspace.\n- wait_for_state: Poll CPU registers until PC equals expectedPC or timeout elapses. Required inputs: none. Optional inputs: expectedPC, timeoutMs, pollMs.\n- nuclear_reset: Kill and restart the VICE process (managed instances only). Required inputs: none.\n- continue_execution: Exit the Binary Monitor and resume CPU execution (BM 0xAA Exit). Required inputs: none.",
